WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.070
This is Centaur.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.651
Once a deal is open, your rep owns the conversation.

3
00:00:06.496 --> 00:00:10.098
Centaur's Analyst keeps the record up to date while they get on with it.

4
00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:15.830
Cody's first call with Northfield Logistics went well, and there's now an open deal.

5
00:00:16.837 --> 00:00:18.566
This morning, Marcus emails again.

6
00:00:19.147 --> 00:00:23.613
He mentions a budget of around forty thousand dollars, says their finance director,

7
00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:25.173
Priya, will need to sign off,

8
00:00:25.173 --> 00:00:28.186
and that they'd like to be live before the end of March.

9
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.968
Oh, and they've had a quote from HubSpot.

10
00:00:32.697 --> 00:00:34.404
Nobody has to type any of that in.

11
00:00:35.342 --> 00:00:37.804
The Analyst reads the email and updates the deal.

12
00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:40.613
The value was blank, so it fills it in.

13
00:00:41.484 --> 00:00:44.536
The close date was blank, so it sets the end of March.

14
00:00:45.474 --> 00:00:48.775
Priya goes into the qualification as the person who signs off.

15
00:00:49.787 --> 00:00:53.922
And HubSpot is added to the deal as a challenger, linked to your battle card.

16
00:00:55.278 --> 00:00:58.627
If Cody had already typed a value, the Analyst wouldn't change it.

17
00:00:59.205 --> 00:01:00.824
It leaves a suggestion instead.

18
00:01:01.715 --> 00:01:03.615
A person's entry always wins.

19
00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:05.921
It also watches for risk.

20
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.677
A new competitor is flagged on the deal, with Marcus's exact words,

21
00:01:10.677 --> 00:01:13.690
so Cody can see what was said, not just a warning.

22
00:01:14.584 --> 00:01:18.236
And when a later email puts that risk to rest, it's marked as dealt with.

23
00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:22.393
It does the same with the notes your reps write after a call.

24
00:01:23.138 --> 00:01:26.485
And every change is listed on the deal's AI updates tab,

25
00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:29.175
so you can see exactly what changed, and why.

26
00:01:31.102 --> 00:01:32.878
The Analyst never sends anything.

27
00:01:33.464 --> 00:01:38.095
If Marcus asks a question, it writes a draft reply and waits for Cody to approve it.

28
00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.374
Centaur CRM.

29
00:01:41.038 --> 00:01:43.515
Deals that stay up to date, without the typing.

30
00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:47.857
Book a demonstration today, at centaurcrm.com.

